):", "D. define name():"], "correct_option": 1, "difficulty": "medium", "marks": 1, "explanation": "Python uses 'def' to define a function, followed by the function name and parentheses."}, {"question_number": 9, "question": "Which of the following is a correct way to create a list in Python?", "options": ["A. list = [1, 2, 3]", "B. [1, 2, 3] = list", "C. list = [1, 2, 3]", "D. list(1, 2, 3)"], "correct_option": 2, "difficulty": "easy", "marks": 1, "explanation": "In Python, a list is created using square brackets, and the syntax [1, 2, 3] is correct."}, {"question_number": 10, "question": "What will happen if you run the following code? x = 10; x = x + 5", "options": ["A. x becomes 15", "B. x becomes 10", "C. x becomes 5", "D. An error occurs"], "correct_option": 1, "difficulty": "easy", "marks": 1, "explanation": "The variable x is updated to the value of 10 + 5, which is 15. So x becomes 15."}], "answer_key": [{"question_number": 1, "correct_option": 2}, {"question_number": 2, "correct_option": 3}, {"question_number": 3, "correct_option": 1}, {"question_number": 4, "correct_option": 1}, {"question_number": 5, "correct_option": 2}, {"question_number": 6, "correct_option": 3}, {"question_number": 7, "correct_option": 1}, {"question_number": 8, "correct_option": 1}, {"question_number": 9, "correct_option": 2}, {"question_number": 10, "correct_option": 1}], "marking_scheme": [{"question_number": 1, "marks": 1}, {"question_number": 2, "marks": 1}, {"question_number": 3, "marks": 1}, {"question_number": 4, "marks": 1}, {"question_number": 5, "marks": 1}, {"question_number": 6, "marks": 1}, {"question_number": 7, "marks": 1}, {"question_number": 8, "marks": 1}, {"question_number": 9, "marks": 1}, {"question_number": 10, "marks": 1}], "status": "assessment_sent_to_students", "metadata": {"api": "tco-assessment-workflow", "mode": "general_knowledge", "assessment_title": "Python Basics Multiple Choice Assessment", "assessment_instructions": "Select the best answer for each